                <pb facs="0188" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg96"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Townsend to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24, 1899</hi></date>.
                        (Received Aug. 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of dispatch No. 7, dated July 10, 1899, and to inform the Department that, in
                    conformity with instructions contained therein, I have urged upon the Belgian
                    Government to so alter the existing regulations in regard to the importation of
                    American cattle that the animals may be slaughtered at any time within ten days
                    from the date of their arrival on Belgian soil. I have also pointed out to the
                    minister for foreign affairs that the present restrictions placed upon the
                    importation of American cattle by the Belgian Government actually prevented such
                    importation and formed a barrier to the development of trade between the two
                    countries.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawrence
                    Townsend.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
